Questions: Would it be better to just m,ake this as an obsidian plugin? or both a theme and a plugin?

> ANSWER (decided 2026-05-31): **Both — theme-first.**
> Build the look as a CSS **theme** that is **Style Settings**-compatible (the Style Settings
> community plugin auto-generates the softness/contrast slider + color pickers from CSS
> comments — no custom plugin needed for those). The theme covers ~90% of the goal,
> including a *default* whole-app background (transparent panes + a body-level background),
> and it can be submitted to community themes on its own.
> Add a **small companion plugin** ONLY for what CSS can't do: the **user-changeable
> background from a local image file** (file picker + persistence) and the **contrast-guard
> auto-scrim** that keeps text ≥ 4.5:1 over any image. The plugin stays optional — users who
> skip it still get the default background.
> Caveat: the graph view is canvas-rendered, so we can set neon *colors* for nodes/edges but
> can't add true per-node glow — plan for "neon colors, light glow," not full bloom.
> Avoid a single all-in-one plugin: it reinvents theming in JS and loses the community-theme
> distribution channel. Full design spec: ./Liquid-Neon-Design-Spec-from-Mythos-Writer.md

